WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.410 --> 00:07.645
Twenty-five years ago, was there someone named

3
00:07.712 --> 00:09.180
Taisuke Sakura working here?

4
00:09.848 --> 00:14.419
Is the world really so full of coincidences?

5
00:16.087 --> 00:17.989
If only you hadn't loved her,

6
00:18.656 --> 00:21.326
you wouldn't have ended up a criminal.

7
00:23.328 --> 00:24.262
KYOKO NOSE

8
00:24.329 --> 00:25.363
I understand.

9
00:25.430 --> 00:29.567
I would like to speak with you too.

10
00:30.068 --> 00:31.836
I'll be waiting.

11
00:46.518 --> 00:47.552
Mariko.

12
00:50.054 --> 00:51.189
Mariko!

13
01:05.570 --> 01:07.839
-Can I look? -Yes.

14
01:11.075 --> 01:13.011
What? This is amazing.

15
01:13.077 --> 01:15.380
You drew this, Fusaido?

16
01:16.247 --> 01:17.215
No, uh…

17
01:19.384 --> 01:20.285
What?

18
01:21.252 --> 01:23.021
I'm Sakura.

19
01:24.022 --> 01:25.990
Taisuke Sakura.

20
01:26.958 --> 01:28.493
Sakura?

21
01:29.527 --> 01:32.230
It's such a wonderful drawing.

22
01:33.565 --> 01:35.266
I love it.

23
01:40.972 --> 01:43.741
A choice between being a police officer or a painter…

24
01:43.808 --> 01:46.911
Oh, that's difficult.

25
01:47.612 --> 01:50.448
But you seem suited for both.

26
01:51.950 --> 01:53.017
You don't mean that.

27
01:53.084 --> 01:55.486
No, I do.

28
01:55.553 --> 01:58.590
You seem like whatever path you decide on, you'll put in the hard work.

29
01:59.824 --> 02:00.892
I'll support you either way.

30
02:08.399 --> 02:09.767
I'm very sorry.

31
02:09.834 --> 02:11.002
I'll get some other flowers.

32
02:11.069 --> 02:13.838
-Forget that. Your hand's more important. -I'm fine, I'm fine!

33
02:13.905 --> 02:14.839
Show me.

34
02:15.740 --> 02:17.742
That's a bit deep, isn't it?

35
02:18.710 --> 02:19.944
Let's go to the hospital.

36
02:48.573 --> 02:49.440
It's done.

37
03:17.802 --> 03:20.605
If you're expecting Mariko, she's not coming.

38
03:34.786 --> 03:35.987
A FEW HOURS EARLIER

39
03:36.054 --> 03:36.888
Mariko.

40
03:37.388 --> 03:40.158
There's something else I need to talk to you about.

41
03:42.327 --> 03:44.028
It's about the secret

42
03:44.762 --> 03:47.398
between me and Sayuri, which you asked about.

43
03:48.433 --> 03:50.501
It was just before it happened with Kyoko.

44
03:51.135 --> 03:53.104
Sayuri, who was my subordinate at the time,

45
03:54.706 --> 03:56.741
told me that Kyoko had been acting strangely

46
03:58.009 --> 04:00.912
and that she might be seeing someone.

47
04:03.214 --> 04:07.018
I took what she said seriously and became suspicious of Kyoko.

48
04:08.319 --> 04:09.687
In the middle of all that,

49
04:11.089 --> 04:13.558
someone attempted to kidnap you,

50
04:14.625 --> 04:17.862
and Kyoko became extremely emotionally unstable.

51
04:19.697 --> 04:22.133
Before the culprit had even been caught…

52
04:25.470 --> 04:27.004
she got into that accident.

53
04:30.808 --> 04:32.243
After she died,

54
04:32.310 --> 04:36.114
this was found in her room.

55
04:39.016 --> 04:40.985
I thought Sayuri

56
04:41.619 --> 04:43.855
had been telling the truth.

57
04:44.455 --> 04:47.692
If it came out that Kyoko had committed suicide after having an affair,

58
04:48.192 --> 04:50.261
it would damage the company's reputation.

59
04:50.928 --> 04:53.798
We didn't want to let the investigation drag on any longer.

60
04:55.867 --> 04:58.069
That's what we discussed together.

61
04:59.170 --> 05:04.108
So, I asked a politician I knew to pull some strings.

62
05:05.042 --> 05:06.277
The investigation?

63
05:07.178 --> 05:08.746
You had them call it off?

64
05:13.751 --> 05:17.789
But I started wondering if Kyoko really could have killed herself.

65
05:19.157 --> 05:21.559
I couldn't shake the feeling that she would never

66
05:22.660 --> 05:24.095
have died and left you behind.

67
05:25.263 --> 05:26.731
What do you mean?

68
05:26.798 --> 05:30.535
Back then, the police also considered that it might not have been an accident…

69
05:33.838 --> 05:37.108
but a murder.

70
05:47.885 --> 05:49.420
TAISUKE SAKURA

71
05:50.455 --> 05:51.622
Yes, hello?

72
05:54.058 --> 05:55.226
Right now?

73
06:00.898 --> 06:02.433
SOTA YUKIMURA: THREE MISSED CALLS

74
06:03.935 --> 06:05.169
SOTA YUKIMURA

75
06:09.340 --> 06:10.174
Hello?

76
06:10.241 --> 06:12.877
Mariko, I'm at your house right now. Where are you?

77
06:15.513 --> 06:16.414
Wait, don't go!

78
06:17.348 --> 06:18.616
What? What happened?

79
06:18.683 --> 06:20.384
I'll explain why later.

80
06:20.451 --> 06:21.652
Please stay at my place.

81
06:22.320 --> 06:26.757
But I already agreed I'd go see him.

82
06:27.391 --> 06:28.326
Where are you?

83
06:29.193 --> 06:30.595
It's that detective, right?

84
06:31.696 --> 06:33.231
Where did you agree to meet him?

85
06:33.898 --> 06:35.600
Is something wrong with Sakura?

86
06:37.535 --> 06:39.504
Give me an explanation!

87
06:42.640 --> 06:44.275
You're always like this!

88
06:44.342 --> 06:46.477
You never tell me the important stuff.

89
06:46.544 --> 06:47.578
Tell me!

90
06:50.915 --> 06:53.184
I-I'll tell you everything later.

91
06:54.852 --> 06:56.053
So please.

92
06:56.654 --> 06:58.022
For now, just trust me.

93
06:59.824 --> 07:00.791
Please.

94
07:14.038 --> 07:15.573
So it was you, Detective.

95
07:16.307 --> 07:18.075
You were the one who killed Tateiwa and Sayuri.

96
07:19.343 --> 07:20.578
Why?

97
07:25.650 --> 07:29.153
Is it because they found out about the secret from 25 years ago?

98
07:29.220 --> 07:30.721
‎FUSAIDO

99
07:39.297 --> 07:41.165
So you found out too?

100
07:53.511 --> 07:55.012
It only happened once.

101
07:57.615 --> 08:02.620
For once in my entire life, I made a mistake.

102
08:04.188 --> 08:06.090
And I've kept it secret…

103
08:08.359 --> 08:09.994
for 25 years too.

104
08:11.829 --> 08:14.065
-Sakura, you got a call on line five. -Okay.

105
08:17.568 --> 08:19.036
Yes, this is Sakura.

106
08:19.103 --> 08:22.940
On that day, that man called me.

107
08:23.441 --> 08:24.675
Who are you?

108
08:25.476 --> 08:27.578
He wouldn't reveal who he was.

109
08:28.412 --> 08:31.015
but he spoke as if he knew the secret…

110
08:33.517 --> 08:35.753
between me and Kyoko.

111
08:39.056 --> 08:43.861
I was waiting to see what kind of man would show up…

112
08:47.498 --> 08:48.633
and you were there.

113
08:50.868 --> 08:55.106
I have evidence that you obtained that partnership through fraud.

114
08:55.172 --> 08:57.174
I can use this.

115
08:58.075 --> 08:59.410
That's what I thought.

116
09:01.912 --> 09:06.751
Someone told me that you may have been frequenting

117
09:06.817 --> 09:09.186
the Nose family home 25 years ago.

118
09:10.554 --> 09:13.491
I heard that the company president's ex-wife, Kyoko,

119
09:13.557 --> 09:18.195
was suspected of having an affair with a younger man.

120
09:19.764 --> 09:20.665
You…

121
09:22.299 --> 09:24.268
were the one she had an affair with,

122
09:25.102 --> 09:27.171
yet 25 years later, you showed up again

123
09:28.005 --> 09:30.207
as a potential marriage prospect for Mariko.

124
09:31.242 --> 09:33.177
What was your goal?

125
09:39.417 --> 09:42.553
You don't need to know anything more than that.

126
09:58.569 --> 10:01.372
Truth is, I didn't want to kill him.

127
10:02.506 --> 10:04.542
No one needs to know

128
10:05.376 --> 10:07.511
about Kyoko and me.

129
10:08.979 --> 10:12.883
But everyone kept fixating on Mariko

130
10:13.718 --> 10:15.753
and probing into our past.

131
10:16.487 --> 10:21.258
Tateiwa, Sayuri, and Yukimura.

132
10:22.426 --> 10:23.961
You too.

133
10:26.731 --> 10:29.266
If you had just quietly taken the fall as the culprit…

134
10:33.704 --> 10:35.706
you wouldn't have had to die.

135
10:57.161 --> 11:01.932
You don't have to watch me that closely. I'm not going anywhere.

136
11:03.234 --> 11:04.268
Sorry.

137
11:05.269 --> 11:06.937
Sota would get mad at me otherwise.

138
11:09.106 --> 11:12.443
What is he trying to do this time?

139
11:13.110 --> 11:14.779
Tomoya, didn't he tell you anything?

140
11:15.312 --> 11:17.548
Absolutely nothing!

141
11:17.615 --> 11:20.518
Then why are you helping him right now?

142
11:21.452 --> 11:22.453
Because we're friends.

143
11:22.520 --> 11:24.555
That's a kindergartner's excuse.

144
11:25.356 --> 11:26.223
Okay then.

145
11:27.324 --> 11:28.425
Want to play cards?

146
11:28.492 --> 11:29.493
-No. -What?

147
11:29.560 --> 11:31.028
Then how about shiritori?

148
11:38.102 --> 11:41.205
Wait, wait, you probably shouldn't look at that…

149
11:44.041 --> 11:44.975
This is…

150
11:47.578 --> 11:48.546
-Kyoko. -Hm?

151
11:48.612 --> 11:50.281
I wanted to give you these today.

152
11:50.781 --> 11:51.882
Here.

153
11:51.949 --> 11:52.783
-What, for me? -Yes.

154
12:12.169 --> 12:14.138
You're a lot like your mother.

155
12:15.539 --> 12:17.408
She was a quiet person,

156
12:18.142 --> 12:21.745
but she was like a sunflower blooming in the family.

157
12:21.812 --> 12:24.415
I painted someone I loved.

158
12:34.725 --> 12:39.296
Wait. Maybe you'd better stop.

159
12:40.764 --> 12:42.666
What was Yukimura investigating?

160
12:43.267 --> 12:45.269
Tomoya, this is important!

161
12:45.336 --> 12:46.537
How is my mother involved?

162
12:46.604 --> 12:49.006
And Tateiwa and Sayuri?

163
12:49.640 --> 12:52.243
I don't really know either,

164
12:52.309 --> 12:55.112
but I think he was investigating everything strange

165
12:55.179 --> 12:57.815
that was happening around you.

166
13:12.997 --> 13:13.931
I have to go.

167
13:14.665 --> 13:16.901
Wait, wait, wait.

168
13:16.967 --> 13:19.770
-Sota said you really had to stay here. -Please!

169
13:20.271 --> 13:22.072
I have to protect Yukimura.

170
13:31.048 --> 13:32.249
Okay. I'm coming too.

171
13:38.222 --> 13:40.357
It's Kyoko that you see in her, isn't it?

172
13:41.725 --> 13:42.993
In Mariko.

173
13:44.795 --> 13:46.964
When I first met Mariko,

174
13:47.698 --> 13:49.633
I thought it was Kyoko standing right there.

175
13:49.700 --> 13:51.635
I was stunned.

176
13:53.237 --> 13:54.505
She is

177
13:56.106 --> 13:58.442
the woman fate intended for me.

178
14:00.678 --> 14:02.880
Which one do you mean?

179
14:05.616 --> 14:07.184
Why did you do that to Kyoko?

180
14:09.720 --> 14:12.289
-You killed her, didn't you? -Because I loved her.

181
14:14.725 --> 14:16.560
You understand, don't you?

182
14:18.662 --> 14:19.997
When the person you love

183
14:20.965 --> 14:24.468
doesn't love you the way you want them to,

184
14:25.302 --> 14:26.837
hatred begins to grow.

185
14:28.339 --> 14:30.975
But I regret it.

186
14:32.242 --> 14:34.044
I was young.

187
14:36.947 --> 14:39.717
So I didn't understand her situation

188
14:40.651 --> 14:42.786
or what she was going through.

189
14:49.193 --> 14:50.294
I'm sorry.

190
14:50.861 --> 14:52.463
I didn't mean it that way.

191
14:54.064 --> 14:57.868
But you said you enjoyed being with me.

192
14:58.802 --> 15:02.306
You said you wished I would deliver flowers every day, didn't you?

193
15:03.240 --> 15:07.911
I was shaken when she suddenly rejected me.

194
15:11.815 --> 15:17.421
She had seemed to accept me.

195
15:19.089 --> 15:23.494
I couldn't understand why she had suddenly changed her mind.

196
15:25.095 --> 15:28.832
After that, she avoided me.

197
15:30.000 --> 15:33.203
I just wanted to talk about it with her.

198
15:33.904 --> 15:35.205
It was you.

199
15:37.174 --> 15:38.609
You kidnapped Mariko.

200
15:39.810 --> 15:40.644
Why…

201
15:43.080 --> 15:45.949
Why? Why? Why!?

202
15:46.583 --> 15:51.422
When I realized she thought I was the kind of person who would kidnap someone…

203
15:54.758 --> 15:57.127
I lost my temper.

204
16:00.497 --> 16:01.532
Forgive me.

205
16:09.406 --> 16:14.778
But after some time had passed and I had calmed down, I understood.

206
16:16.080 --> 16:19.249
She was much older than me.

207
16:20.384 --> 16:22.386
She had her own situation in life,

208
16:24.221 --> 16:28.425
so, of course, she couldn't accept me.

209
16:30.861 --> 16:31.995
But…

210
16:34.932 --> 16:37.935
I couldn't understand that back then.

211
16:40.971 --> 16:42.873
Don't mess with me!

212
16:49.613 --> 16:52.382
I've only heard about Kyoko from your perspective,

213
16:52.449 --> 16:55.119
so I don't know her feelings at all,

214
16:55.185 --> 16:57.254
I don't, but…

215
16:58.288 --> 17:01.658
the Kyoko I knew was an incredibly bright, friendly person.

216
17:02.192 --> 17:05.662
If someone regularly visited her,

217
17:05.729 --> 17:09.333
of course, she would be polite enough to reach out

218
17:09.399 --> 17:11.068
and make them feel welcome, right?

219
17:12.402 --> 17:13.971
What are you talking about?

220
17:14.538 --> 17:16.473
She always looked at my paintings.

221
17:17.141 --> 17:18.542
They made her happy.

222
17:19.143 --> 17:21.044
She said she was my number-one fan.

223
17:21.678 --> 17:24.414
-She said she'd cheer me on! -That's right!

224
17:24.481 --> 17:26.416
She was cheering you on!

225
17:26.483 --> 17:27.918
But nothing more!

226
17:29.153 --> 17:32.556
She was struggling with her relationship with her husband!

227
17:34.892 --> 17:36.260
That's why I…

228
17:41.632 --> 17:42.499
Excuse me.

229
17:44.201 --> 17:45.169
Delivery.

230
17:47.971 --> 17:48.805
Here you are.

231
17:48.872 --> 17:50.474
Thank you.

232
17:51.775 --> 17:53.277
Are you okay?

233
18:00.083 --> 18:01.752
This cheers me up.

234
18:03.487 --> 18:04.955
So pretty.

235
18:11.662 --> 18:14.598
I had to protect her.

236
18:18.902 --> 18:22.406
But even assuming Kyoko was struggling with her husband,

237
18:22.472 --> 18:24.741
that doesn't mean she loved you.

238
18:26.143 --> 18:28.378
She never asked you to save her.

239
18:30.214 --> 18:32.849
What you consider kindness was frightening to her.

240
18:42.626 --> 18:44.328
Well, I guess I was the same.

241
18:48.398 --> 18:50.033
Even though she never asked me to,

242
18:51.602 --> 18:53.370
I thought I had to protect her or help her.

243
18:57.207 --> 19:00.844
I never once made the mistake of thinking she liked me, though.

244
19:01.912 --> 19:03.647
That's not true.

245
19:04.681 --> 19:07.351
I was only trying to help her.

246
19:09.486 --> 19:10.487
Forgive me.

247
19:11.922 --> 19:13.323
So…

248
19:14.358 --> 19:17.361
I didn't do anything to frighten her!

249
19:19.529 --> 19:22.399
She must have loved me.

250
19:25.068 --> 19:26.069
After all…

251
19:29.706 --> 19:32.209
After all, she's the woman fate intended for me.

252
19:37.281 --> 19:38.115
Yukimura?

253
19:38.181 --> 19:39.316
Sota?

254
19:39.383 --> 19:40.884
Stay away!

255
19:43.820 --> 19:45.088
Yukimura…

256
19:51.762 --> 19:52.796
See?

257
19:54.464 --> 19:56.066
She came after all.

258
20:04.908 --> 20:06.076
Kyoko.

259
20:08.578 --> 20:10.314
Why are you looking at me like that?

260
20:12.616 --> 20:16.887
I just love you, that is all.

261
20:18.655 --> 20:19.823
I am…

262
20:21.925 --> 20:23.293
Mariko.

263
20:30.334 --> 20:31.601
Why…

264
20:36.373 --> 20:37.708
Stay back!

265
20:39.710 --> 20:41.345
We're the same, aren't we?

266
20:47.718 --> 20:48.919
You understand, don't you?

267
20:56.927 --> 20:57.994
Wait!

268
21:00.230 --> 21:03.500
Look, I found this among my mother's belongings.

269
21:05.068 --> 21:07.704
I think it was meant for you, Sakura.

270
21:24.554 --> 21:28.825
Thank you for the beautiful painting the other day.

271
21:28.892 --> 21:30.560
I'll treasure it.

272
21:31.561 --> 21:35.732
Your painting feels as though your pure,

273
21:35.799 --> 21:38.969
honest heart is reflected in it.

274
21:39.035 --> 21:40.937
It's very moving.

275
21:47.677 --> 21:49.780
I hope that you can continue to live on,

276
21:51.481 --> 21:55.152
ten years from now, 20 years from now,

277
21:56.420 --> 22:00.390
in the wonderful life that you want,

278
22:01.758 --> 22:03.427
with that same heart.

279
22:25.816 --> 22:27.050
Long time no see.

280
22:49.406 --> 22:52.008
I wonder what can change the nature of a man.

281
22:55.879 --> 22:59.549
No, maybe it never changes.

282
23:01.351 --> 23:03.320
This man was always a straightforward,

283
23:04.554 --> 23:06.189
pure-hearted person.

284
23:11.495 --> 23:13.430
But he made some kind of mistake.

285
23:14.831 --> 23:18.835
Or maybe to him, he had been wrong the entire time.

286
23:21.037 --> 23:22.706
Without realizing it,

287
23:23.340 --> 23:25.609
he'd reached a point of no return.

288
23:25.675 --> 23:28.245
TAISUKE ARRESTED ON SUSPICION OF MURDER

289
23:28.812 --> 23:30.914
She really is so much like her.

290
23:30.981 --> 23:35.519
In the end, the letter from Kyoko that Mariko found

291
23:35.585 --> 23:37.454
was what made Sakura turn himself in.

292
23:38.688 --> 23:39.523
Someday…

293
23:39.589 --> 23:43.793
Through her own strength, Mariko regained her safety.

294
23:44.728 --> 23:46.963
I just wanted to protect Kyoko.

295
23:52.836 --> 23:54.070
Mariko.

296
23:56.673 --> 23:58.675
I wanted to protect Mariko.

297
24:00.010 --> 24:03.747
I found evidence that Tateiwa was misappropriating company expenses

298
24:03.813 --> 24:05.682
and illegally accessing the company's system.

299
24:05.749 --> 24:09.786
I couldn't protect Mariko anymore.

300
24:10.420 --> 24:14.858
No, I never needed to protect her in the first place.

301
24:14.925 --> 24:17.294
I figured if Mariko's safety was at risk,

302
24:17.961 --> 24:19.596
I had to do something.

303
24:20.196 --> 24:21.298
With that in mind…

304
24:25.902 --> 24:30.874
I've been watching over Mariko Nose for 25 years.

305
24:32.375 --> 24:37.647
I wrote about Mariko and everything else that is relevant to the case.

306
24:45.655 --> 24:48.024
We'd like to take this as reference material

307
24:48.091 --> 24:49.659
for the investigation.

308
24:50.560 --> 24:51.494
Okay.

309
24:53.964 --> 24:54.965
What would you like to do?

310
24:55.832 --> 24:58.268
Will you file a police report against Sota Yukimura?

311
25:01.137 --> 25:02.072
He's the man…

312
25:04.307 --> 25:07.344
who saved my daughter's life.

313
25:09.613 --> 25:11.247
I don't want him punished.

314
25:16.586 --> 25:18.588
-Thank you. -Thank you.

315
25:18.655 --> 25:20.390
-Put the PCs in here as well. -Okay.

316
25:21.658 --> 25:24.828
Because Mariko and the president chose not to press charges,

317
25:24.894 --> 25:27.297
I was not held criminally responsible.

318
25:29.032 --> 25:30.000
But…

319
25:31.201 --> 25:34.137
it was time for me to take responsibility for what I'd done.

320
25:40.276 --> 25:41.911
RESIGNATION LETTER

321
25:45.148 --> 25:47.817
You said you'd explain everything later.

322
26:00.397 --> 26:02.399
My 25-year love…

323
26:04.367 --> 26:05.535
is over.

324
26:30.293 --> 26:31.628
You were straightening them up!

325
26:31.695 --> 26:35.632
Even though you know I was fixing them, you still put them down the wrong way?

326
26:35.699 --> 26:37.300
-Yes. -"Yes"?

327
26:37.367 --> 26:39.269
You're being annoying!

328
26:39.335 --> 26:40.470
You're one to talk.

329
26:46.009 --> 26:48.144
When did I go wrong?

330
26:57.987 --> 26:58.922
I see.

331
27:00.557 --> 27:01.691
I guess, from the beginning…

332
27:19.409 --> 27:20.810
She was trying to do something bad.

333
27:22.212 --> 27:23.313
It can't be helped.

334
27:37.127 --> 27:40.163
The last time I spoke to Sayuri…

335
27:41.865 --> 27:44.467
she bowed and asked me to take care of you.

336
27:48.071 --> 27:51.674
Now that we can't hear her tell her own story anymore,

337
27:51.741 --> 27:53.443
I don't know what's true.

338
27:54.878 --> 27:55.812
But

339
27:56.412 --> 27:59.249
one thing I know for sure is that she cared deeply about you

340
28:00.750 --> 28:04.220
and wanted you to be happy.

341
28:09.759 --> 28:11.895
This house hasn't exactly been

342
28:12.996 --> 28:16.800
a comfortable place for you two, has it?

343
28:18.802 --> 28:20.937
Thinking I had to protect you,

344
28:21.504 --> 28:23.773
I kept acting behind the scenes, on my own.

345
28:24.874 --> 28:29.245
I never told either of you anything that actually mattered.

346
28:31.247 --> 28:34.484
I care about both of you, Mariko…

347
28:37.020 --> 28:38.488
and you, Keito,

348
28:39.889 --> 28:41.858
more than anyone.

349
28:43.827 --> 28:45.461
You're both adults now.

350
28:46.396 --> 28:48.865
Maybe you don't need me anymore.

351
28:50.934 --> 28:54.537
But I want this to be a place you can always come back to.

352
29:00.143 --> 29:01.544
Hear that?

353
29:02.412 --> 29:03.479
What?

354
29:04.113 --> 29:05.515
You too.

355
29:06.082 --> 29:07.517
Don't act like you're the only one who's grown up.

356
29:07.584 --> 29:09.185
I am an adult.

357
29:09.786 --> 29:13.089
How about I make dinner tonight?

358
29:14.991 --> 29:18.061
-Mariko, you'll eat with us, right? -Yes.

359
29:18.127 --> 29:19.495
I'll help.

360
29:20.630 --> 29:21.898
I'll help too.

361
29:28.471 --> 29:31.207
-Where should I put these? -Hm? Oh, just there's fine. Okay, Grandma.

362
29:33.109 --> 29:36.112
-Let's do this for now. -Yes.

363
29:36.179 --> 29:38.748
ONE YEAR LATER

364
29:38.815 --> 29:40.516
-Here? -Here.

365
29:40.583 --> 29:41.718
-Over here. -Yes.

366
29:41.784 --> 29:44.287
-What do you think? -For this, is this part okay?

367
29:44.354 --> 29:45.722
-Or… -I'm not sure.

368
29:45.788 --> 29:48.057
-Yeah. Like that is good. -Move it a little bit forward.

369
29:48.124 --> 29:49.125
Like this? How's this?

370
29:51.194 --> 29:52.795
Okay, here we go.

371
29:52.862 --> 29:57.033
Three, two, one, start.

372
29:57.600 --> 29:59.102
Hello!

373
29:59.168 --> 30:01.704
Welcome to the official Velel account!

374
30:05.141 --> 30:08.211
People are really pouring in.

375
30:08.278 --> 30:09.812
Thank you very much!

376
30:10.346 --> 30:15.151
It's finally launching today, Velel's Aurelie Adieu Serum.

377
30:16.386 --> 30:17.253
MENTION ITS BEST SELLING POINT!

378
30:17.320 --> 30:22.025
This serum contains some of the hottest ingredients right now,

379
30:22.091 --> 30:24.227
including stem cell culture supernatant and PDRN.

380
30:24.794 --> 30:26.663
Let's show them the texture.

381
30:27.263 --> 30:31.067
-Ah, shall we try it out then? -Yes.

382
30:31.134 --> 30:32.235
Cheers.

383
30:32.302 --> 30:35.004
-Cheers! -Cheers!

384
30:35.071 --> 30:36.940
-All right. -Good work, everyone!

385
30:38.441 --> 30:41.911
All right, everyone, we've got a special menu today.

386
30:41.978 --> 30:44.948
-It's all on the house. -Thank you very much!

387
30:45.014 --> 30:47.050
Tomoya, you keep giving us stuff.

388
30:47.116 --> 30:49.185
You'll go bankrupt, you know?

389
30:49.252 --> 30:51.154
She's telling you off.

390
30:51.220 --> 30:56.459
Okay then, Sara, I guess I shouldn't give you a special fruit juice.

391
30:56.526 --> 30:59.595
What? No, no! Please!

392
30:59.662 --> 31:00.863
Just kidding. Let's pick one.

393
31:01.431 --> 31:02.699
What would you like?

394
31:04.133 --> 31:07.337
You've got such a great boyfriend, Izumi.

395
31:07.904 --> 31:11.174
If I get married, I'd want someone like that too.

396
31:11.941 --> 31:14.644
Right, Mariko, have you been looking for a partner--

397
31:15.144 --> 31:16.579
What, I can't say that?

398
31:18.448 --> 31:19.882
What do you mean?

399
31:20.683 --> 31:23.686
You don't have to treat me like I'm fragile.

400
31:24.787 --> 31:28.691
Actually, lately I've been thinking I'd rather just stay single.

401
31:29.258 --> 31:32.195
I don't dislike being alone in the first place.

402
31:32.261 --> 31:33.629
I enjoy my work.

403
31:35.198 --> 31:39.535
Mariko, I'm sure you'll find the happiness you want.

404
31:41.070 --> 31:42.672
What? Asai?

405
31:42.739 --> 31:44.340
How long have you been here?

406
31:44.407 --> 31:45.742
Listen.

407
31:45.808 --> 31:49.512
Everyone can have the life they want.

408
31:50.613 --> 31:52.648
You can have it!

409
31:52.715 --> 31:54.650
Wait, Asai, is that alcohol?

410
31:55.551 --> 31:57.653
Well, is it? Is it?

411
31:57.720 --> 31:58.821
Zucchini?

412
32:03.960 --> 32:05.495
She's putting on a brave face.

413
32:07.130 --> 32:09.699
Everyone has to go through a breakup eventually, right?

414
32:12.568 --> 32:15.204
I'm scared, you know.

415
32:16.973 --> 32:20.943
Once I have something precious, I start imagining the day I lose it.

416
32:21.544 --> 32:25.748
It's like a countdown begins in my heart.

417
32:29.152 --> 32:29.986
It's scary.

418
32:35.124 --> 32:36.893
But I want to be with you, Izumi.

419
32:40.396 --> 32:44.167
Even if you break up someday, it's better to have met someone at all.

420
32:45.234 --> 32:48.237
How about we treasure the happy times we have together?

421
32:50.973 --> 32:53.009
Shouldn't you say we're never going to break up?

422
32:53.776 --> 32:56.345
I don't make promises about things I can't know for sure.

423
32:57.880 --> 32:59.015
I'm leaving now.

424
32:59.082 --> 33:01.584
-See you later! -See you.

425
33:38.688 --> 33:39.622
Good morning.

426
33:39.689 --> 33:41.491
-Ah, good morning! -Good morning!

427
33:41.557 --> 33:42.625
Perfect timing! Come here!

428
33:43.392 --> 33:44.894
-I want to ask you something. -Yes?

429
33:44.961 --> 33:45.661
VIDEO CALL

430
33:45.728 --> 33:48.297
If you press this, you'll be able to see the other person while you talk.

431
33:48.364 --> 33:49.599
-Whoa! -Like this.

432
33:49.665 --> 33:52.902
Wow! Thank you.

433
33:52.969 --> 33:55.104
-Thanks as always. -No problem.

434
33:55.171 --> 33:57.306
-I'll be going now. -Okay, thank you!

435
33:57.974 --> 33:59.475
-Hey, hold on! -Here!

436
33:59.542 --> 34:01.944
-What! -How's this?

437
34:02.011 --> 34:03.546
-Amazing! -Are you sure? It's a lot.

438
34:03.613 --> 34:04.580
Yes, it's okay!

439
34:04.647 --> 34:06.115
-Wow, thank you! -Hey, Yuki,

440
34:06.182 --> 34:08.284
have you gotten used to life around here?

441
34:08.351 --> 34:12.889
Well, I feel really comfortable here, like I've been here all my life.

442
34:13.823 --> 34:16.359
Like I lived here in a past life.

443
34:16.425 --> 34:17.793
I've been in this town for a year.

444
34:20.363 --> 34:23.332
The people here call me Yuki.

445
34:23.399 --> 34:24.200
TOMIYA COOPERATIVE FISH MARKET

446
34:25.034 --> 34:26.903
It's the first nickname I've ever had in my life.

447
34:29.038 --> 34:29.972
It's not a bad feeling.

448
34:30.473 --> 34:32.475
‎REGARDING THE LOG-IN ERROR

449
34:33.976 --> 34:36.479
I thought I needed to disappear from Mariko's world.

450
34:38.080 --> 34:42.385
I thought that meant losing everything I had.

451
34:43.052 --> 34:45.388
Yuki! Have a drink with us! Come in!

452
34:45.454 --> 34:47.823
I can't. I have work.

453
34:47.890 --> 34:50.159
-Just one beer! -Surprisingly, that wasn't the case.

454
34:50.226 --> 34:52.795
-Come on! -I can live here in this town.

455
34:52.862 --> 34:55.398
This fish is delicious.

456
34:57.466 --> 34:58.568
‎Not bad, right?

457
35:00.903 --> 35:02.038
The food is great.

458
35:02.805 --> 35:04.040
The people are kind.

459
35:05.007 --> 35:06.108
It's not bad.

460
35:06.175 --> 35:08.477
That's what I'm saying! You get it, don't you?

461
35:08.544 --> 35:10.046
I'm not sure I do.

462
35:10.112 --> 35:11.814
You have to actually say it!

463
35:11.881 --> 35:13.482
What's wrong with you all?

464
35:13.549 --> 35:16.519
My goodness, you never say what's important out loud!

465
35:18.688 --> 35:21.090
-You know… -You never put it into words.

466
35:21.157 --> 35:22.058
Now, now…

467
35:26.662 --> 35:30.866
I didn't think there'd be anything worth writing in a diary anymore.

468
35:30.933 --> 35:34.870
But it turns out you can find things worth remembering everywhere.

469
36:23.252 --> 36:26.856
She looks like Mariko.

470
36:34.463 --> 36:37.033
Am I finally hallucinating?

471
36:42.972 --> 36:44.540
That's really her, isn't it?

472
36:45.274 --> 36:46.709
What is Mariko doing here?

473
36:47.443 --> 36:50.279
There's no way a coincidence like this could happen in my life.

474
36:50.346 --> 36:52.682
This is crazy. This is bad!

475
36:53.182 --> 36:54.283
She'll think I'm still following her!

476
37:06.595 --> 37:08.964
-I'm sorry. -I'm sorry.

477
37:09.031 --> 37:10.900
I told you to watch out.

478
37:12.735 --> 37:13.569
What?

479
37:13.636 --> 37:16.072
-Why? Why? Why are you here? -A coincidence.

480
37:16.138 --> 37:17.873
-Really, it's a coincidence. -What?

481
37:17.940 --> 37:20.509
-There's no way this is a coincidence! -There is!

482
37:20.576 --> 37:22.278
What are you doing here, Mariko?

483
37:23.179 --> 37:25.448
Well, there's a golf course near here.

484
37:25.514 --> 37:27.416
I used to visit it with my father.

485
37:29.618 --> 37:30.986
Wait, what about you?

486
37:31.053 --> 37:31.954
What are you doing here?

487
37:34.924 --> 37:38.094
I'm… living here.

488
37:41.230 --> 37:42.431
What?

489
37:45.234 --> 37:46.469
See you.

490
38:36.285 --> 38:37.753
ADHESIVE BANDAGE

491
38:39.422 --> 38:41.390
FESTIVAL

492
38:41.457 --> 38:42.391
ENTRANCE EXAM ADMISSION TICKET

493
39:47.523 --> 39:48.357
Mariko!

494
39:53.896 --> 39:59.935
You are my first love and the person I admire.

495
40:02.137 --> 40:04.573
And you've given me a lot of happiness.

496
40:06.575 --> 40:07.676
As long as…

497
40:09.745 --> 40:11.614
you were just there,

498
40:12.715 --> 40:14.416
I didn't need anything else.

499
40:16.952 --> 40:19.154
That alone made me happy.

500
40:21.390 --> 40:22.558
But, to be honest,

501
40:23.926 --> 40:24.760
I was hoping

502
40:25.261 --> 40:28.964
we'd eventually meet by coincidence, and we'd become close and be able to talk.

503
40:29.732 --> 40:32.868
Somewhere in my heart, I think I was hoping

504
40:33.969 --> 40:35.471
for something like fate.

505
40:37.406 --> 40:39.842
Something that convenient would never happen to me, of course.

506
40:40.609 --> 40:45.080
I thought I'd just keep living my life how I have been.

507
40:50.052 --> 40:51.153
But then one day,

508
40:52.621 --> 40:56.859
I thought you might actually get married someday,

509
40:56.926 --> 40:58.761
and I couldn't just sit still.

510
40:59.828 --> 41:01.730
I ended up impulsively talking to you.

511
41:04.567 --> 41:07.836
The real you is more careless than I expected,

512
41:08.504 --> 41:11.006
and I never know what you're thinking.

513
41:13.509 --> 41:17.513
But even more than when I was just watching you on social media,

514
41:17.580 --> 41:20.015
even more than when I was making up my own version of you,

515
41:20.916 --> 41:24.486
after getting to know the real you,

516
41:25.220 --> 41:28.857
I came to love you much, much more.

517
41:36.198 --> 41:37.166
I loved you.

518
41:38.233 --> 41:41.403
I'd always loved you, for 25 years.

519
41:43.005 --> 41:46.008
I was always selfish, and I made mistakes and everything.

520
41:47.910 --> 41:50.045
But the fact that I fell in love with you…

521
41:52.648 --> 41:54.049
was never a mistake.

522
41:59.722 --> 42:00.856
Thank you.

523
42:05.194 --> 42:09.398
You are not my destiny.

524
42:11.667 --> 42:12.601
Correct.

525
42:13.736 --> 42:16.105
I used to think the same thing.

526
42:17.873 --> 42:21.310
That if we met by coincidence, got along by coincidence,

527
42:22.745 --> 42:24.246
and somehow found each other,

528
42:25.514 --> 42:28.384
it would mean you were my destiny.

529
42:30.986 --> 42:32.888
But I know that's wrong.

530
42:35.491 --> 42:37.693
We can meet in some completely unremarkable way,

531
42:39.328 --> 42:41.397
nothing special at all.

532
42:42.297 --> 42:44.299
And as we casually spend more time together,

533
42:45.534 --> 42:50.072
we get to know each other and have memories together.

534
42:50.839 --> 42:52.141
And then,

535
42:52.207 --> 42:55.944
after spending years, and decades side by side,

536
42:56.445 --> 43:00.716
maybe one day we'll look back and think, "That person really was my destiny."

537
43:03.452 --> 43:04.887
That's what I think now.

538
43:10.159 --> 43:11.060
So…

539
43:16.932 --> 43:19.168
You are not my destiny.

540
43:24.873 --> 43:25.708
Not yet.

541
43:29.845 --> 43:30.679
What?

542
43:42.291 --> 43:43.392
You dropped it.

543
43:47.596 --> 43:48.430
Wait, this…

544
43:49.465 --> 43:50.299
This is my…

545
43:51.500 --> 43:52.401
How?

546
43:53.936 --> 43:54.837
It's a secret.

547
43:58.440 --> 43:59.274
Wait!

548
43:59.341 --> 44:01.977
What kind of life are you living here?

549
44:02.044 --> 44:03.212
Are you living well?

550
44:03.278 --> 44:04.146
Well…

551
44:05.013 --> 44:08.317
I'll show you around.

552
44:09.485 --> 44:12.421
Do you think you have a choice, like not showing me around?

553
44:13.088 --> 44:13.989
Nope!

554
44:14.056 --> 44:15.090
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
